## 5. Database Design

The system uses **MongoDB Atlas** with three collections, designed for auditability, cacheability, and prompt versioning.

### 5.1 Collection: `prompts`

Stores versioned LLM prompt templates, enabling prompt iteration without code changes.

| Field | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `_id` | ObjectId | MongoDB auto-generated ID |
| `name` | String | Unique prompt identifier (e.g., "claim_extraction") |
| `version` | Integer | Version number for tracking iterations |
| `template` | String | The prompt template with `{variable}` placeholders |
| `description` | String | Human-readable description |
| `variables` | Array[String] | List of template variables |
| `is_active` | Boolean | Whether this version is currently active |
| `created_at` | DateTime | Creation timestamp |
| `updated_at` | DateTime | Last modification timestamp |

**Indexes:** Unique compound index on `(name, version)`, lookup index on `(name, is_active)`.

### 5.2 Collection: `fact_checks`

Stores complete fact-check results for every pipeline run.

| Field | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `_id` | ObjectId | MongoDB auto-generated ID |
| `article_text` | String | Full input article text |
| `article_hash` | String | SHA-256 hash for deduplication |
| `claims` | Array[String] | Extracted claims |
| `evidence` | Array[Object] | Search results per claim (query, raw_results, timestamp) |
| `verdicts` | Array[Object] | Per-claim verdict, confidence, and justification |
| `credibility_score` | Float | Aggregated article score (0.0 - 1.0) |
| `model_used` | String | LLM model identifier |
| `prompts_used` | Object | Prompt names/versions used in this run |
| `duration_seconds` | Float | Total pipeline execution time |
| `created_at` | DateTime | Timestamp of the fact-check |

**Indexes:** Index on `article_hash` (for dedup), index on `created_at` (for history queries).

### 5.3 Collection: `search_cache`

Caches DuckDuckGo search results to reduce redundant API calls and improve latency.

| Field | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `_id` | ObjectId | MongoDB auto-generated ID |
| `query_hash` | String | SHA-256 hash of the search query |
| `query` | String | Original search query text |
| `results` | String | Raw search results |
| `cached_at` | DateTime | When the result was cached |
| `expires_at` | DateTime | TTL expiry (auto-deleted by MongoDB) |

**Indexes:** Unique index on `query_hash`, TTL index on `expires_at` (auto-purges after 24 hours).

### 5.4 Entity Relationship Diagram

```mermaid
erDiagram
    PROMPTS {
        ObjectId _id PK
        string name
        int version
        string template
        bool is_active
        datetime created_at
    }

    FACT_CHECKS {
        ObjectId _id PK
        string article_text
        string article_hash
        array claims
        array evidence
        array verdicts
        float credibility_score
        string model_used
        float duration_seconds
        datetime created_at
    }

    SEARCH_CACHE {
        ObjectId _id PK
        string query_hash UK
        string query
        string results
        datetime expires_at
    }

    FACT_CHECKS ||--o{ SEARCH_CACHE : "references cached evidence"
    FACT_CHECKS }o--|| PROMPTS : "uses active prompts"
```

