## 8. Sample Output

### Input Article
> "The Indian government announced today that it will launch a ₹10,000 crore fund to support AI startups. According to the Finance Minister, the first grants will be disbursed by December 2026. The initiative aims to create 50,000 new jobs in the AI sector over the next three years."

### Output (JSON)
```json
{
  "_id": "6a46d2f14ae85433370e0a0b",
  "claims": [
    "The Indian government will launch a ₹10,000 crore fund to support AI startups",
    "The first grants from the fund will be disbursed by December 2026",
    "The initiative aims to create 50,000 new jobs in the AI sector over the next three years"
  ],
  "verdicts": [
    {
      "claim": "The Indian government will launch a ₹10,000 crore fund to support AI startups",
      "verdict": "NOT_ENOUGH_INFO",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "justification": "No relevant information found in search results to support or refute the claim."
    },
    {
      "claim": "The first grants from the fund will be disbursed by December 2026",
      "verdict": "NOT_ENOUGH_INFO",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "justification": "No search results found to address the claim."
    },
    {
      "claim": "The initiative aims to create 50,000 new jobs in the AI sector over the next three years",
      "verdict": "NOT_ENOUGH_INFO",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "justification": "No search results found to address the claim."
    }
  ],
  "credibility_score": 0.5,
  "duration_seconds": 10.54
}
```

> **Note:** The sample article is fictional, so the system correctly returns NOT_ENOUGH_INFO with 0.0 confidence for all claims — demonstrating that the v2 prompts avoid false verdicts.

